(25604, 'delsut', 'mechanical-engineering', 1, 'Mechanical Engineering', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '(i) Two (2) \'A\' Level passes from Chemistry, Physics and Mathematics. (ii) ND upper credit, NCE technical and HND in Mech. Engineering.', 'Five (5) SSC credit passes to include Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics, English Language and any other Science subject.', 'Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(25605, 'delsut', 'fine-arts-and-industrial-design', 1, 'Fine Arts and Industrial Design', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'National Diploma (ND) at credit level in Fine Art from any recognized polytechnic.National Diploma (ND) with a Pass level in Fine Art from any recognized polytechnic. However, to be admitted into 200 Level, a candidate with a Pass must have two years industrial experience after graduation. Diploma in Fine Art from Fine and Applied Art Programme in Delta State University of Science and Technology, Ozoro or any other university. A\' Level passes in Fine Art and at least one other subject shall be admitted into 200 Level.Higher National Diploma (HND) at credit level from any recognized polytechnic shall be admitted into 300 Level.', 'Candidates seeking admission into degree programme (B.A. Fine Arts and Industrial Design) must have five (5) 0\' Level credits. These include English Language, Mathematics and any other three subjects in Senior School Certificate Examination or its equivalent in not more than two sittings. For holders of NTC, the relevant subjects could be General Wood work, Building/Engineering Drawing, Introduction to Building Construction; Decorative Painting; Spray Painting, Lining, Sign and Design; Wall hanging, Colour Mixing/Matching and Glazing; Printing Origination; Machine Printing and Finishing; General Metal Work, Basic Electricity, Spinning, Weaving, Surface Design and Printing; Bleaching, Dyeing and Finishing; Graphic Design; Graphic Printing and Ceramics.', 'Candidate must write English Language and any other three (3) subjects.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(25606, 'delsut', 'environmental-management', 1, 'Environmental Management', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Candidates who fulfill the normal admission requirements and who have obtained GCE, A\' Level, HSC/IJMB or equivalent passes in Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Mathematics, or Geography and any ether subject noted above may be admitted at the 200 level of the programme.Candidates who have obtained National Diploma (ND) in Environmental Management or any related course (with minimum of Lower Credit) or other approved equivalent qualifications by the Federal Ministry of Education and the University Senate rnav be admitted into 200 Level.Higher National Diploma (HND) at credit level from any recognized polytechnic shall be admitted into 300 Level.', 'The minimum academic requirement is credit level passes at not more than two sittings in five (5) subjects at O\'Level in nationally recognized examination including English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and any other subjects from Geography, Economics, Biology, Technical Drawing, Fine Art, Government, Civic Education, Agriculture, Further Mathematics, History, Social Studies or any other relevant/related subject.', 'Candidate must register and write English Language, Mathematics and any two (2) of Geography, Economics, Physics, Chemistry, Biology or any other relevant subject.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(25607, 'delsut', 'surveying-and-geoinformatics', 1, 'Surveying and Geoinformatics', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Candidates who satisfy the UTME requirements and in addition have G.C.E (A/Level) passes in Mathematics and physics and any of geography, technical drawing, fine arts, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Agricultural Science, and who Holds a National Diploma ND (Lower Credit ) in related discipline may be admitted into 200 level. Holders of Higher National Diploma HND in surveying and geoinformatics with at least Lower credit plus O\' level requirements may be admitted into 300 level of the programme.', 'Senior Secondary School Certificate (SSCE), General certificate of Education (GCE) and National Examination council ( NECO) SSCE with credit level passes in at least five (5) subjects in not more than two (2)sittings: three of which must be in English Language, Mathematics and Physics; While two must be from Geography, Technical Drawing, Chemistry, Further Mathematics Economics Biology, Fine Arts, Building Construction and Agricultural Science.Note: Chemistry is not compulsory as an O/L requirement for admission', 'Mathematics, Physics, English Language and any other subject from the following: Chemistry, Biology, Agricultural Science, Economics, Geography, Fine Arts Technical Drawing and Elementary Surveying <w:LsdExce', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(25608, 'delsut', 'estate-management', 1, 'Estate Management', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Candidates seeking direct entry admission into the degree programme must fulfill all the UTME admission requirements. Have obtained G.C.E. Advanced level, H.S.C/IJMB or equivalent passes in at least two relevant subjects drawn from the UTME subject grouping, including Economics. NOTE: ND and HND applicants from Estate Management and other relevant disciplines such as Surveying, Quantity Surveying, Building Technology, Cartography, Town Planning, Architecture and Environmental Management may be considered for direct entry admission into 200 and 300 Levels respectively provided they satisfy the minimum UTME requirements for admission.', 'The minimum academic requirement is credit level passes at not more than two sittings in five (5) subjects at O\' Level in nationally recognized examination including English Language, Mathematics, Economics and any other two (2) subjects one of which must be a science subject from Biology Chemistry, Physics, Agricultural Science, Geography, Technical Drawing, Computer Science, Business Studies, Commerce and Financial Accounting.', 'Candidate must register and write English Language, Mathematics, Economics and any other one (1) subject from; Biology Chemistry, Physics, Agricultural Science, Geography, Technical Drawing, Computer Science, Business Studies, Commerce and Financial Accounting. <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" SemiHidden=\"true\" UnhideWhenUsed=\"true\" Name=', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(25609, 'delsut', 'public-administration', 1, 'Public Administration', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Two (2) \'A\' Level passes chosen from Economics, Accounting, Business Management, Government, Geography and Statistics.', 'Five (5) SSC credit passes to include English Language, Economics and Government. For NBC holders, the other relevant subjects could be from any of the following: Accounting, Principles of Accounts, Commerce, Office Practice and Secretarial Duties.', 'Government, Economics and any other subject.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
