(26182, 'babcock', 'architecture', 1, 'Architecture', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Five SSC credit passes, two of which must be at the advanced level or candidates who hold National Diploma in a relevant field may be admitted into the 200 Level to study Architecture. Holders of Higher National Diploma (HND) in a relevant field may also be admitted into 300 - Level if they have Upper Credit or Distinctions.', 'Four (4) year Programme admission: In addition to UTME score, the candidate should possess five credit passes in Mathematics, English Language, Physics and two other subjects from the following: Chemistry, Biology, Technical Drawing, Fine Arts, Geography, Economics, Building Construction and Land Surveying at not more than two sittings.', 'English Language, Mathematics, and Physics and any one of the following subjects: Chemistry, Geography, Fine Arts, or Technical Drawing', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(26183, 'babcock', 'estate-management', 1, 'Estate Management', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Candidates seeking direct entry admission into the degree programme shall: Fulfil all the UTME admission requirements besides JAMB. Have obtained G.C.E. Advanced level, H.S.C/IJMB or equivalent passes in at least two relevant subjects drawn from the UTME subject grouping, including Economics or Geography. ND and HND applicants from Estate Management and other relevant disciplines such as Surveying, Cartography, Town Planning, Architecture and Environmental Management may be considered for direct entry admission into 200 and 300 Levels provided they satisfy the minimum requirements for admission via UTME as stated above.', 'Five (5) year Programme admission: In addition to acceptable scores in UTME, candidates seeking UTME admission into the five-year B.Sc. degree programme in Estate Management must have obtained five Senior Secondary Certificate (SSC) credit passes which must include Mathematics, English Language and Economics. In addition to the three mandatory subjects mentioned above, two other subjects are required which are to be drawn from Geography, Chemistry, Physics, and Biology; or, ONE subject from Geography, Chemistry, Physics, and Biology, and ONE from Business Studies, Commerce, Agricultural Science and Technical Drawing.', 'Mathematics, English Language and Economics. Two other subjects are to be drawn from Geography, Chemistry, Physics, and Biology; or, ONE subject from Geography, Chemistry, Physics, and Biology, and ONE from Business Studies, Commerce, Agricultural Science and Technical Drawing.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(26184, 'babcock', 'electrical-electronics-engineering', 1, 'Electrical / Electronics Engineering', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For four-year Direct Entry, in addition to five (5) Senior School Certificate (SSC) credit passes which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry, candidates with at least two passes in relevant subjects (Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry) at the GCE Advanced Level or IJMB or JUPEB may be considered for admission. Candidates with good National Diploma (ND) results in relevant Engineering Technology programmes may also be considered for admission into 200 levels. Holders of upper credit pass and above at Higher National Diploma (HND) level, are eligible for consideration for admission into 300 level.', 'For the five-year degree propgramme, in addition to acceptable passes in the Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME), the minimum admission requirement is credit level passes in Senior School Certificate Examination (SSCE) in at least five subjects, which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(26185, 'babcock', 'mechanical-engineering', 1, 'Mechanical Engineering', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For four-year Direct Entry, in addition to five (5) Senior School Certificate (SSC) credit passes which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry, candidates with at least two passes in relevant subjects (Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry) at the GCE Advanced Level or IJMB or JUPEB may be considered for admission. Candidates with good National Diploma (ND) results in relevant Engineering Technology programmes may also be considered for admission into 200 level. Holders of upper credit pass and above at Higher National Diploma (HND) level, are eligible for consideration for admission into 300 level.', 'For the five-year degree propgramme, in addition to acceptable passes in the Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME), the minimum admission requirement is credit level passes in Senior School Certificate Examination (SSCE) in at least five subjects, which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(26186, 'babcock', 'civil-engineering', 1, 'Civil Engineering', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For four-year Direct Entry, in addition to five (5) Senior School Certificate (SSC) credit passes which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry, candidates with at least two passes in relevant subjects (Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry) at the GCE Advanced Level or IJMB or JUPEB may be considered for admission. Candidates with good National Diploma (ND) results in relevant Engineering Technology programmes may also be considered for admission into 200 level. Holders of upper credit pass and above at Higher National Diploma (HND) level, are eligible for consideration for admission into 300 level.', 'For the five-year degree propgramme, in addition to acceptable passes in the Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME), the minimum admission requirement is credit level passes in Senior School Certificate Examination (SSCE) in at least five subjects, which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(26187, 'babcock', 'computer-engineering', 1, 'Computer Engineering', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For four-year Direct Entry, in addition to five (5) Senior School Certificate (SSC) credit passes which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry, candidates with at least two passes in relevant subjects (Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry) at the GCE Advanced Level or IJMB or JUPEB may be considered for admission. Candidates with good National Diploma (ND) results in relevant Engineering Technology programmes may also be considered for admission into 200 level. Holders of upper credit pass and above at Higher National Diploma (HND) level, are eligible for consideration for admission into 300 level.', 'For the five-year degree propgramme, in addition to acceptable passes in the Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME), the minimum admission requirement is credit level passes in Senior School Certificate Examination (SSCE) in at least five subjects, which must include English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and other acceptable science subjects at not more than two sittings.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
