(28185, 'bsu', 'doctor-of-pharmacy', 1, 'Doctor of Pharmacy', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28186, 'delsu', 'agribusiness-management', 1, 'Agribusiness Management', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28187, 'delsu', 'doctor-of-pharmacy', 1, 'Doctor of Pharmacy', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28188, 'iaued', 'agriculture', 1, 'Agriculture', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Two passes at the Advanced level or two NCE passes not lower than Merit; one of the merit passes must be in Agricultural science/Biology/Health science/ Animal husbandry/Fisheries.', 'Five Credit passes in WASC/NECO/ GCE in English Language, Mathematics, and any three of Agricultural Science/BiologyChemistry, Physics, Animal husbandry, Fisheries, Economics.', 'English language, Chemistry and two of Agricultural Science, Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Animal husbandry, Fisheries, Economics, Geography, Book Keeping.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28189, 'iaued', 'banking-and-finance', 1, 'Banking and Finance', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Candidates seeking admission through direct entry are expected to possess, in addition to credit level passes in English Language, Mathematics, Economics or Commerce and any two from the following subjects: Government, Book-Keeping, Accounting, History, CRK, Business Methods, Typewriting, Literature in English, Biology, at least credit in National Diploma certificate or three year NCE programme width passes in Accounting and or related subject areas such as Finance, Banking, Marketing and Management.', 'Five (5) O\'level credits in English Language, Mathematics, Economics/Commerce and any other two subjects from Government, Book-Keeping, Accounting, History, C.R.K, Business Methods, Typewriting, Literature in English, Biology etc', 'English Language, Mathematics, Economics and Government.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28190, 'iaued', 'educational-technology', 1, 'Educational Technology', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Applicants with one of the following qualifications may be considered for admission by direct entry: (a). A minimum of five (5) credit passed at not more than two sittings at credit level of the SSCE/ GCE O/level. No of subjects shall be counted at both ordinary and advance levels. (b). Credits or merits in three major subject areas in the NCE. (c). Two passes at JUPEB, IJMB, OND, HND or Cambridge moderated schools of basic studies terminal examination or international Baccalaureates from recognised institution.', 'The department requirement for B.ED four (4) years degree programme includes five (5) credits ordinary level in English language, Mathematics and any other three (3) relevant subjects to the candidates option in Arts, Science, Social Science and Vocational in not more than two sittings at the WASC/SSCE/GCE/NECO or their equivalents.', 'English Language and other three subjects relevant to the candidates option in Arts, Science, Social Science and Vocational', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28191, 'iaued', 'entrepreneurship', 1, 'Entrepreneurship', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Direct Entry applicants should possess five credit passes in SSCE/WAEC/GCE, at least two of which at Advanced level in relevant subjects or equivalent examinations like NABTEB, JUPEB, IJMB etc. The subjects include: English Language, Mathematics, Economics or Commerce or Marketing or Entrepreneurship, and any other two from Government, Accounts, Book-keeping, Office Practice, Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Store Management, Business method, Agricultural Sciences, Salesmanship, Christian Religious Knowledge, Geography, Short-hand, literature in English, Biology, Insurance, I C T, Data processing, Store Keeping, Book Keeping, Tourism, Stenography, Civic Education, etc. ii) ND, NCE etc in relevant disciplines with at least upper credit grade in addition to the five credit passes as stated in (i) above. iii) Final certificate of relevant professional bodies in addition to five credit passes as stated in (i) above.', '(i) Candidates should obtain in NOT MORE THAN TWO SITTINGS, a minimum of five relevant CREDITS passes in SSCE/NECO/GCE/\'O\' LEVEL examinations or equivalent examinations. The relevant subjects shall include English Language, Mathematics, Economics or Commerce or Marketing or Entrepreneurship, and any two of the following subjects: Salesmanship, Government, Accounts, Book-keeping, Office Practice, Store Management, Business method/Studies, Agricultural Sciences, Christian Religious Knowledge, Geography, Short-hand, Literature in English, Biology, Chemistry, Insurance, ICT, Data processing, Store Keeping, Tourism, Civic Education, etc . Such candidate shall be admitted into year one of the degree programme in the department. (ii) Equivalent passes at \'O\' level in other recognized examinations in Nigeria and elsewhere may be considered by the department, subject to approval by the University.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Economics or Commerce etc', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28192, 'iaued', 'employment-and-human-resource-management', 1, 'Employment and Human Resource Management', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In addition to the O\' Level requirements stipulated in UTME above, a candidate must have passed at credit level in at least two A\' Level papers in the basic subjects required for the programme.A candidate with ND in a relevant area such as Diploma in Industrial Relations and Personnel Management (IRPM), Diploma in Business Administration (DBA), Public Administration and or any other Diploma certificates with Upper Credit in addition to the requirements for UTME.A candidate with HND in a relevant discipline with at least Upper Credit in addition to the requirements for UTME.A candidate with a B.Sc./BA or any other first degree, with a minimum of a 3rd Class in addition to the requirements for UTME. A candidate with the minimum score acceptable by the University in JUPEB, in addition to the requirements for UTME.', 'A candidate must obtain at least a Credit level pass in five subjects at the O\' Level/SSCE examinations of WAEC, NECO or any other body accepted by the University in not more than two sittings in subjects including Mathematics, English and any of the following: Economics, Commerce, Government/Civic Education, Financial Accounting and Marketing.', 'English Language, Mathematics, Economics or Commerce', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(28193, 'iaued', 'social-work', 1, 'Social Work', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Five O\'Level Credits including English Language and Mathematics At least merit pass or lower credit in NCE/OND', 'English language, Mathematics , Any 3 of the following: Government, Economics, Geography, Commerce, Civic EducationHistoryLiterature in EnglishChristian Religious StudiesIslamic StudiesBusiness StudiesMarketingBookkeepingData processingAgricultural ScienceMusicHealth EducationFrenchAnimal husbandry and Any of the science subjects', 'English language, Government, Economics, Religious Studies, or any other arts subjects.', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
